<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Asbestos testing in Geelong answers the question that has to come first: is the material actually asbestos? You cannot settle that from the colour of a sheet, the look of a fence, or the age of the house. Under Victoria's OHS Regulations, only a laboratory approved by NATA can analyse a sample and identify asbestos. A test is the honest first step, not a formality.</p><p>It is also the cheap step. Victorian and national labs publish $88 to $160 per sample, and most houses need three to eight samples, because every different material has to be tested separately. A negative result means you get on with the job. A positive one means you know what you are dealing with before anyone picks up a grinder, and we can put you in touch with licensed asbestos removalists who quote the work themselves. Call now and get it tested before you touch it.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">A sample from every different material</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A fence, an eaves lining and a bathroom wall sheet are three samples, not one. Most houses need three to eight, and larger properties can run to eight or twelve.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Analysed by a NATA-accredited laboratory</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Victoria's OHS Regulations allow only an approved asbestos laboratory to identify asbestos in a sample. Endorsed reports carry the NATA insignia, and you can check any lab at nata.com.au.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Results in 1 to 5 business days</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">That is the standard turnaround Victorian and national labs publish. A 24 to 48 hour result is usually available for a surcharge of 25% to 50%.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">A written result, not an opinion</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">The report states whether asbestos was detected in the sample submitted and what type it is. It is a document you can hand to a builder, a buyer or a removalist.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Indicative prices before you commit</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Lab analysis runs $88 to $160 per sample. An on-site inspection with sampling is a Melbourne-metro benchmark of $395 to $900, and there is no published Geelong rate anywhere.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">A clear next step either way</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">If it comes back positive, we put you in touch with licensed asbestos removalists. Their WorkSafe Victoria licence number appears on every quote, and you deal with them directly.</p>
      </div>
</div>
